13307	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s9","entry":{"id":"review-78a3e868357b6dfea05a30fadda117a9","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T06:41:11.853Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac2/ac3: the existing tracker setting (type github vs none) is the switch for creating issues at first draft in a repo with no team policy, with no new setting","evidence":"docs/plans/team-workflow.md:310 records the user's 2026-10-23 decision: issues are created at first draft in a repo with no team policy whenever the tracker setting is on; a repo with tracker none makes no tracker call (ac3). The LLD's §2.1 and §3.4 implement exactly this. [files: docs/plans/team-workflow.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac5 ('when a git pull or push completes') is met by refreshing after the daemon's git_pull / git_push tools plus an explicit refresh","evidence":"DEF s9 ac5: 'when a git pull or push completes … the tracker's status is refreshed'. The design hooks only src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts and push.ts, so git run in a terminal or IDE never triggers it. The design admits this in its open question, and docs/plans/team-workflow.md:311 shows the question is 'not yet answered'. The explicit refresh surface is also not named: the existing explicit path, src/cli/services/workflow.ts:410-411 `sync()`, calls syncTracker directly rather than the new bounded refreshTrackerStatus. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json, docs/plans/team-workflow.md, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Get the user's answer to open question 2 before planning. State which surface (CLI sync, IPC or MCP) is the explicit refresh, and whether `sync()` in cli/services/workflow.ts moves onto refreshTrackerStatus.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today ensureDraftIssues returns not-applicable/no-team-policy for a repo with no policy or teamMode false, making no tracker call","evidence":"src/workflow/draft-issues.ts:110 `if (policy.value === 'none' || !policy.value.teamMode) return { status: 'not-applicable', reason: 'no-team-policy' };`, which comes before any loadTracker call (line 125). [files: src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"syncTracker today reads issue state through ghGetIssueState (no runGh timeout) and lenient resolveGithubConfig, and writes epicStatus/storyStatus/lastSyncedAt via patchTrackerMeta","evidence":"src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts:38-60 uses resolveGithubConfig, ghAuthOk, ghGetIssueState and then patchTrackerMeta(defineJson, { epicStatus, storyStatus, lastSyncedAt }). src/workflow/tracker/github.ts:317-318: ghGetIssueState uses `out('gh', [... '--json','state,labels'])`, which has no timeout option, unlike runGh (line 92, timeout GH_TIMEOUT_MS). [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A dry-run git_push returns success with data.pushed false; a dry-run git_pull only fetches; a failed git command returns fail() before any post-step","evidence":"push.ts:118 returns fail on a non-zero code; push.ts:124 sets `pushed: !dryRun` with success true (line 135). pull.ts:67-79: dryRun routes to `git fetch` and returns early; pull.ts:91 returns fail on a non-zero code. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused: runGh with a 10-second timeout and a classified failure (missing-tool / missing-signin / unreachable / rejected) is available for readIssueStatus","evidence":"github.ts:49 GH_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000. github.ts:68-80 classifyGhFailure maps ENOENT to missing-tool, ETIMEDOUT/SIGTERM to unreachable, sign-in text to missing-signin, and anything else to rejected. github.ts:86 runGh is exported and the adapter already imports it (github-adapter.ts:38). [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The widened hook reads the tracker setting with resolveGithubConfig (the reader the terminal approve uses), and creation then works through the existing loadTracker path","evidence":"ensureDraftIssues loads the port with loadTracker (draft-issues.ts:125). loadTracker resolves the target with the strict resolveStrictTrackerTarget (github-adapter.ts:315; config/github.ts:349-388), and its header says it 'is for team features only' (github-adapter.ts:9-11). The strict reader refuses configs that the lenient resolveGithubConfig/resolveEntry accepts: for example, an entry with no type falls through to a 'type none' refusal at github.ts:372. A repo with no team policy can therefore pass the 'tracker is on' check and still get not-ready from loadTracker, whereas the terminal approve (tracker-auto.ts:85-97 gate, which uses createGithubTracker) would succeed. Moving syncTracker onto loadTracker also adds a whoAmI call and the strict refusal for every solo repo. [files: src/workflow/draft-issues.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"Choose one reader for both the on/off check and the port construction in repos with no team policy: either the lenient createGithubTracker path that tracker-auto uses, or state that the strict loader is intended and that a lenient-only config becomes not-ready. Add a test for the disagreement case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding 'status-read' needs three edits: the Capability union (port.ts:21), ALL_CAPABILITIES (port.ts:127) and the GitHub adapter's CAPABILITIES (github-adapter.ts:57); without the ALL_CAPABILITIES edit missingCapabilities never reports it","evidence":"port.ts:21 is the union; port.ts:127-131: `missingCapabilities` filters ALL_CAPABILITIES, so a capability absent from that list is never reported. github-adapter.ts:57 declares the set. loadTracker (github-adapter.ts:318-320) returns a rejected result naming the missing capability. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac7's shown tracker record is changed at src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts:24-37 (TrackerMeta)","evidence":"refs.ts:51-60 TrackerMeta is the stored meta.tracker type, which the design says gains no stored field. What the chain report shows is ChainReport.tracker at src/workflow/chain.ts:67-69 ({ pushed, epicRef? }), built at chain.ts:228-233 and rendered at chain.ts:373. That site is not listed. Adding derived fields to the stored TrackerMeta interface would let patchTrackerMeta/carryTracker persist them. Separately, patchTrackerMeta is quoted as returning void, but refs.ts:111 returns TrackerMeta. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/chain.ts]","action":"List chain.ts (the ChainReport.tracker type, its builder and renderer) and any artifact display as the ac7 change sites. Add artifactId and revision to the shown type, not to the stored TrackerMeta. Correct the patchTrackerMeta signature.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored field is added: the refresh writes only epicStatus, storyStatus and lastSyncedAt through patchTrackerMeta as a meta-only atomic write, and existing tracker fields are kept","evidence":"refs.ts:111-120: patchTrackerMeta merges through carryTracker (every key of the patch wins, units merge key by key) and writes with writeArtifact(jsonPath, artifact, 'meta-only'). TrackerMeta already has epicStatus, storyStatus and lastSyncedAt (refs.ts:57-59), so no schema change is needed. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding readIssueStatus to the sc1 port is a methodAdd amendment owned by s1, not a redesign; s1 explicitly deferred the issue-status read to this extend","evidence":"The s1 adjacent-scope text says: 'Syncing tracker status on git pull and push, and an issue-status read on the port, are deferred to the define extend.' port.ts:116 shows the same optional-method pattern already used for an addition (readSignoffRequest?, s8). [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Overriding constraint k4 for issue creation in repos with no team policy is authorised and does not redesign s4's sc3 hook beyond this one behaviour","evidence":"docs/plans/team-workflow.md:310: k4 'does not cover issue creation', by the user's decision. The change is confined to the policy branch at draft-issues.ts:110; the team-repo path (lines 112-140) is unchanged. [files: docs/plans/team-workflow.md, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The refresh after git_pull/git_push is bounded (30 s deadline plus at most one 10 s gh call), and a slow tracker only delays the result","evidence":"The tools' execute is async (pull.ts:59, push.ts:80) and runs in the daemon, but syncTracker/refreshTrackerStatus are synchronous and runGh uses execFileSync (github.ts:86-93, `_exec = execFileSync`). For up to 40 s the refresh blocks the daemon's event loop, so IPC, the queue and other tool calls stall. The design states the bound but not this blocking effect or how to avoid it. Each loadTracker call also adds a whoAmI gh call (github-adapter.ts:322) that the deadline accounting does not mention. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"State whether the refresh runs off the event loop (for example deferred after the tool result, or through an async exec), or accept and document the blocking. Count the whoAmI call inside the deadline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A malformed github.json or an unexpected throw in the hook becomes not-ready and never undoes the draft","evidence":"draft-issues.ts:141-144: a catch-all turns any throw into notReady(..., 'rejected', ...), so a GithubConfigError from the new resolveGithubConfig read would already become not-ready. The design's explicit mapping (§2.1, §5) is consistent with this. [files: src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac8 maps to at least one runnable test at the stated level","evidence":"§6's acceptance mapping covers ac1-ac8. The seams exist: the exec seam _setTrackerExecForTests (github.ts:31) records the timeout option for the contract test; DraftHookDeps.readPolicy/loadTracker (draft-issues.ts:55-58) cover the unit tests; the existing redraft-preserves-tracker.test.ts:77-88 already drives syncTracker through a fake gh. ac8 can only be shown with an injected fake port, because loadTracker always builds the GitHub adapter (github-adapter.ts:317). The design's tests use an injected loader, which is adequate. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/redraft-preserves-tracker.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":4,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T06:41:11.853Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
