13977	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s9","entry":{"id":"review-75980ce8f7af3a6bc637dc4447c3d04e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T06:52:02.150Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers ac1–ac8 of DEF s9 and builds no non-goal; the k4 override and the 120 s timeout are the user's recorded decisions","evidence":"DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json s9 lists ac1–ac8 (team draft, solo draft with tracker on, no tracker = nothing, no duplicate on terminal approve, refresh on pull/push plus explicit refresh, git still completes, issue key + artifact id + revision, non-GitHub tracker). docs/plans/team-workflow.md:310 records the k4/ac2 decision, :315 the accepted blocking, :316 the 120 s timeout and the 240 s bound, :317 the lenient path and putting ac7 on ChainReport.tracker. Each one maps to a section of the LLD. [files: docs/plans/team-workflow.md, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac7 ('an issue the daemon has created for an artifact … carries the issue key, the artifact id and a revision') is met by adding artifactId/revision to ChainReport.tracker for the Define only","evidence":"chain.ts:227-235 readTrackerMeta builds the record from the Define and the Epic's issue only (unitIssueOf(repoPath, epicHash)). ac7 is per artifact, but the design also creates Story issues (ensureDraftIssues for an LLD/plan covers [epic, story], draft-issues.ts:76-78). No Story or Task artifact is shown with its issue key, artifact id and revision. The design covers only the Epic's Define. [files: src/workflow/chain.ts, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"Either show issue key, artifact id and revision for each Story head that has an issue (e.g. per-story entries in the chain report), or record in team-workflow.md that ac7 is satisfied by the Epic record alone.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today ensureDraftIssues returns not-applicable (no-team-policy) for any repo without a team policy, uses the strict loadTracker otherwise, and never throws","evidence":"draft-issues.ts:108-110: `if (policy.value === 'none' || !policy.value.teamMode) return { status: 'not-applicable', reason: 'no-team-policy' }`; :125 `(deps.loadTracker ?? loadTracker)(repoPath, new Set(['issue-create']))`; :141-144 a catch-all turns any error into not-ready. [files: src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"syncTracker today reads issue state with ghGetIssueState (bypassing the port and runGh) and writes epicStatus/storyStatus/lastSyncedAt via patchTrackerMeta","evidence":"sync.ts:47-60 calls ghAuthOk(), then ghGetIssueState(owner, repo, ref) for the Epic and each Story, mapIssueStatus, then patchTrackerMeta(defineJson, { epicStatus, storyStatus, lastSyncedAt }). github.ts:317-318 ghGetIssueState uses the legacy out() with no timeout. [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_push returns success with data.pushed false on a dry run, and git_pull's dry run is a fetch that returns success; failed git commands return fail() early","evidence":"push.ts:116-135: early `fail(...)` on code≠0; `pushed: !dryRun`; `success: true`. pull.ts:67-78: the dryRun branch runs `git fetch` and returns success; :89-91 a failed pull returns fail() early. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readIssueStatus, the status-read capability, refreshTrackerStatus and the tracker.refresh IPC method are new; createGithubTracker, runGh, GH_TIMEOUT_MS, missingCapabilities/ALL_CAPABILITIES and patchTrackerMeta exist with the stated shapes","evidence":"Searching src for `tracker\\.refresh|refreshTrackerStatus|readIssueStatus|status-read` finds nothing. port.ts:21 Capability union is 'claim'|'issue-create'|'signoff-request'|'completion'; :127 ALL_CAPABILITIES; :130 missingCapabilities filters it. github-adapter.ts:57 CAPABILITIES = {claim, issue-create, signoff-request}; :257 createGithubTracker(owner, repo). github.ts:49 GH_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000; :86 runGh classifies failures; :76 builds 'gh timed out after N s'. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The no-team-policy draft path reuses the same on/off check and lenient port as the terminal approve (resolveGithubConfig + createGithubTracker)","evidence":"tracker-auto.ts:85-97: gate() calls resolveGithubConfig, skips on type none or GithubConfigError, then ghAuthOk. :177-181: trackerGate returns createGithubTracker(g.cfg.owner, g.cfg.repo). unit-issue.ts:237 also reads resolveGithubConfig. Note: the terminal path also runs ghAuthOk, which the hook does not. A signed-out gh therefore surfaces in the hook as a create failure (missing-signin from runGh), which the LLD's error paths cover. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The explicit refresh inventory is complete: 'the existing explicit sync' is sync() in cli/services/workflow.ts, plus a new tracker.refresh IPC method","evidence":"cli/services/workflow.ts:410-411 sync() → syncTracker. There is a second explicit sync path the LLD does not name: the `tracker.sync` workflow (runners/tracker/context.ts:114-139, assembleSyncContext). It calls requireGithubAdapter(resolveGithubConfig(...)) directly. chain.ts:325-328 recommends exactly this path as the 'sync-tracker' next action. That path stays GitHub-only and off the port and the deadline, which conflicts with ac8 and with 'one function'. [files: src/workflow/runners/tracker/context.ts, src/workflow/chain.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"State what happens to the tracker.sync workflow: route it through refreshTrackerStatus, or change the chain report's sync-tracker next action to the new refresh. Otherwise record that it is left as is and why.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The change sites for adding status-read and moving GH_TIMEOUT_MS to 120_000 are complete","evidence":"Existing tests pin the old values and will fail. port.test.ts:173 `assert.deepEqual([...r.value.capabilities].sort(), ['claim','issue-create','signoff-request'])`. github-adapter.test.ts:62 `/timed out after 10 s/`, :85 `assert.equal(GH_TIMEOUT_MS, 10_000)`, :92/:94 timeout 10_000. setup.test.ts:202 `timeout, 10_000`. github-adapter.test.ts:219-220 checks the capability set. None of these is listed among the LLD's call sites or test changes. [files: src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/port.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/github-adapter.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/setup.test.ts]","action":"Add these test files to the change sites and the test strategy: update the expected capability set and the 10 s timeout assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The git tools can 'add a warning to the result' within the existing ToolResult contract","evidence":"daemon/tools/types.ts:33-48: ToolResult is { output, format, success, error?, data? }. There is no warning field. The LLD (2.7, 2.8, 5) says the refresh failure is 'added as a warning' but does not say where it goes (appended to output, or a field on data). The integration tests assert 'adds a warning' against an unspecified shape. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/pull.ts]","action":"Specify the carrier, e.g. a `trackerRefresh` / `warnings` entry on data plus a line appended to output, and name it in the tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored shape changes: TrackerMeta is unchanged, artifactId/revision on ChainReport.tracker are derived at read time, and a missing meta.revision reads as 0","evidence":"chain.ts:67-71 ChainReport.tracker is a computed report type. :227-235 readTrackerMeta derives it from the Define head and unitIssueOf, so adding derived fields changes no stored record. sync.ts:60 writes only epicStatus/storyStatus/lastSyncedAt through patchTrackerMeta, and the LLD keeps exactly those. The revision-0 default is the existing sc3 rule (s4). [files: src/workflow/chain.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The port change is proposed as an amendment to s1's sc1 rather than a redesign, and nothing owned by s4/s5 is redesigned","evidence":"The LLD §4 states that sc1 is consumed and readIssueStatus is proposed as a methodAdd amendment owned by s1. The s1 adjacent scope in the HLD says 'an issue-status read on the port [is] deferred to the define extend', which is this Story. legacy-exec.test.ts:25 marks ghGetIssueState 'deferred to the status-sync story'. The team gate (sc4) and the issue-creation code (sc3) are reused unchanged (draft-issues.ts keeps ensureUnitIssueDetailed). The GH_TIMEOUT_MS change retargets an HLD non-functional line, and the LLD says it is done by amendment (team-workflow.md:316). [files: src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/legacy-exec.test.ts, docs/plans/team-workflow.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every tracker call in the refresh is bounded, so refreshTrackerStatus returns within 240 s ('a started gh call is bounded by its own 120-second runGh timeout … the sign-in check counts inside the deadline')","evidence":"The only sign-in check syncTracker uses today is ghAuthOk (sync.ts:47). It runs `silent('gh', ['auth','status'])` (github.ts:168-175), the legacy exec with NO timeout. legacy-exec.test.ts:23 pins ghAuthOk as retained on the legacy path. The 240 s bound and the 'Every tracker command now has a 120-second timeout' summary hold only for calls through runGh. If the refactored syncTracker keeps ghAuthOk, the refresh after git_pull/git_push can block without bound. [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/legacy-exec.test.ts]","action":"State that the refresh's sign-in check is the port's whoAmI (ghCurrentLogin → runGh, github.ts:558-559) or that ghAuthOk moves onto runGh. Narrow the summary's 'every tracker command' wording to runGh calls, or move the remaining legacy calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A malformed github.json in a no-policy repo is detectable as GithubConfigError and can be turned into not-ready","evidence":"config/github.ts:200-203 documents that resolveGithubConfig throws GithubConfigError when github is enabled but no owner/repo resolves. tracker-auto.ts:89-90 and sync.ts:42 already catch it by instanceof. Separately, draft-issues.ts:141-144's catch-all would already make any other throw not-ready. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1–ac8 maps to at least one runnable (unit/contract/integration) test, with smoke only as an extra","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping gives each of ac1–ac8 a unit, contract or integration test. ac2 and ac5 also carry a smoke test, but each has a unit or integration test as well. The fixtures exist: the exec seam _setTrackerExecForTests (github.ts:31) records options such as timeout (github-adapter.test.ts:92), fake TrackerPort objects are the existing pattern (draft-issues.test.ts:50), and DraftHookDeps.loadTracker is injectable (draft-issues.ts:55-59). The gap on the ac7 scope is reported under coverage-of-intent. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/draft-issues.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":5,"low":10,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T06:52:02.150Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
